     "intro": "Dei Gratia in the fifth day (\"Dei Gratia no Rashinban\")<br />\r\n<br />\r\n\"By what means could those girls have escaped the depths of the sea alive.<br />\r\nPerhaps, had they made other choices, the result may have been different?\"<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAugust 1st 2033<br />\r\nA deep sea cruise submarine sinks to the <br />\r\nmurky ocean floor 700m below the surface<br />\r\n<br />\r\n50 lives were lost in an instant.<br />\r\nThe remaining passengers, left to figure out the path to their survival.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBut, at the depths of the ocean, there <br />\r\nexisted a threat they had never imagined.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAn eternal replay of records and memories...<br />\r\nCan the fragment of \"two survivors\", save them in the end?<br />\r\n<br />\r\n\"Who lives, who dies, you are the one that decides.\"<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThis is a novel game with no correct answer."
    }
